  "description": "Computer-Aided Manufacturing: the CAD to CAM to G-code software pipeline that converts digital part geometry into machine-executable toolpaths. Covers toolpath strategy selection (2D contouring, 3D parallel/adaptive clearing, climb vs conventional milling), post-processing for machine-specific G-code dialects, and feed/speed optimization by material. Bridges digital CAD design and physical CNC execution.",
